# Portal Three-Zone Layout

- For this portal project, treat the usable page width under the top banner as the real layout boundary.
- Default portal pages to a three-zone frame: left utility rail, stable center canvas, right utility rail.
- Keep the center canvas clean and width-stable for data content; do not shrink it just because side content exists.
- Put filters, search, selectors, and setup controls in the left rail when they are present.
- Put notes, recommendations, calls to action, explanations, or user guidance in the right rail when they are present.
- If a side rail has no content, keep the structural space so it reads as intentional margin rather than collapsing the page inward.
- Do not solve width requests by compacting the main content inside an inherited max-width container when the page should instead expand to the full banner-aligned frame.
